# TanStack Start (Cloudflare Workers)

`apps/web` is the only web deployable, hosted on Cloudflare Workers via `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` and Wrangler.

## Routes and data

- Route files coordinate URL parsing, loaders, pending/error states, metadata, and feature composition. They do not contain competitive rules or persistence queries.
- Prefer SSR loaders and server functions for initial authorized data (first paint, redirects, permission-gated bootstrap).
- **Client calls to `/api/v1` use TanStack Query** (`useQuery` / `useMutation` or module hooks). Do not add new `useEffect` + fetch for product endpoints. See [ADR-0012](/docs/adr/0012-tanstack-query-client-server-state.md).
- `queryFn` / `mutationFn` call same-origin `*BrowserClient` helpers (or equivalent). Never import use cases, D1, or provider adapters from presentation.
- Keys live under `apps/web/src/shared/presentation/query/query-keys.ts`. Invalidate related keys after mutations.
- Validate all route params, search params, form data, and HTTP bodies at the inbound boundary.
- Keep filters, selected encounter, tab, and shareable view state in typed URLs when users expect deep links.
- Permission-specific data is selected on the server. Hiding controls is presentation only.
- Freshness aids trigger an authorized refetch; never merge untrusted broadcasts into canonical state.

## Server entrypoints

- Product server functions, `/api/v1/*` BFF routes, queue consumers and cron handlers reach `apps/api` through the existing SDK/service boundary. Product use cases and adapters are composed in `apps/api/src/di`, not in the web Worker.
- Auth routes proxy to the separate auth Worker via `AUTH_SERVICE`; SSR/BFF session resolution uses that same binding (ADR-0015).
- Server-only modules, secrets, D1/R2 clients, and provider SDKs must not enter client bundles.
- Read Worker bindings from `env` / composition — do not assume Node `process.env` at module scope on Workers.
- Durable EA sync work is persisted and queued before the request returns.
- Map expected failures to typed safe responses with `code`, `messageKey`, and `requestId`.

## Rendering and UX

- Preserve loading, empty, stale, permission, and recoverable-error states across SSR and hydration.
- Avoid client-only rendering for public landing/portal content that benefits from SEO.
- Encounter detail uses deep links appropriate to current desktop/mobile patterns in `design.md`.

Use the current root scripts for build and preview; deploy only within the requested scope. For new pages or blocks, apply the matching repo creation skill and its Storybook workflow.
